        {
            "id": "19808438",
            "user": "WikiHowUser20230227233914",
            "timestamp": "00:41, 13 March 2016",
            "anon": false,
            "size": "(7,866 bytes)",
            "change": -313,
            "summary": "(RCP reverted edits by 72.208.219.111 (talk) to  revision #19801179 by Anna)",
            "is_minor": false,
            "is_expert": false,
            "status": "reverted",
            "contribution_type": "revert",
            "reverted_by": "Jax Smith",
            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "Swimming pools are a great addition to a big back yard, creating a great way to spend time together as a family and get in some super fun exercise! It isn't the easiest building project, however. The average cost of a swimming pool, even if you're building it yourself, is about $25,000. Keep in mind that in most cities, you will not be allowed to build the pool yourself as you need to be a certified and licensed builder in order for the pool to be considered up to code. With these things in mind, get started with Step 1 to see what you can expect from the building process."
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "Swimming pools are a great addition to a big back yard, creating a great way to spend time together as a family and get in some super fun exercise! It isn't the easiest building project, however. The average cost of a swimming pool, even if you're building it yourself, is about $25,000. Keep in mind that in most cities, you will not be allowed to build the pool yourself as you need to be a certified and licensed builder in order for the pool to be considered up to code. However, you can save yourself a lot of money, around 30-40%, by hiring your own licensed contractors and avoiding the middle man, large pool building companies. A good example can be found at http://www.ourpoolbuild.com. With these things in mind, get started with Step 1 to see what you can expect from the building process.",
                    "*http://www.ourpoolbuild.com Contributing source - How we built our own pool and saved 30%"
                ]
            }
        },
